Pauravi—Pauravi; Rohini—Rohini; Bhadra—Bhadra; Madira—Madira; Rochana—Rochana; Ila—Ila; Devaki—Devaki; Pramukhah—Principal;
Ch—Thus; Asan—Thine; Palyah—Wives; Aanakadundubheh—Aanakadundubhi, meaning Vasudeva's. Devaki, Pauravi, Rohini, Bhadra, Madira, Rochana, Ila, etc., were the wives of Anakadundubhi (Vasudeva). Among them, Devaki was prominent. Balam, Gadam, Saranam, Cha, Durmadam, Vipulam, Dhruvam. Vasudevastu Rohinyam Krutadinudapayat. 46. Meaning of the word

Balam—strength; Gadam—fist; Saaranam—support; Cha—also; Durmadam—dull; Vipulam—abundant; Dhruvam—eternal;
Vasudevah—Vasudeva (Krishna's father); Tu—indeed; Rohinyam—from Rohini's womb; Krita-Adin—created; Adin—sons;
Udapayitvam—produced. Vasudeva produced Bal, Gad, Saran, Durmad, Vipul, Dhruva, Kritta, and other sons from the womb of his wife Rohini. Subhadro, Bhadrabahu, Durmado, and Bhadra. The twelve elements are born from the earth. 47). Nandopanandaka, Krishnadvaipayana, and others.
Kaushalya, with her hair, is the one who is the moon of the Kulananda. 48. Meaning of the word

Subhadrah - Subhadra; Bhadrabahuh - Bhadrabahu; Cha-tatha; Durmadah - Durmad; Bhadrah - Bhadra; Eva - without doubt; Cha - also; Paurvyaah - named Paurvi; Tanayah - son; Hi - without doubt; Ete - all these; Bhuta-Aadyaah - named Bhuta etc.; Dvadasha - twelve; Abhavan - originated; Nand-
Upanand-Krutak-Shur-Aadyaah - Nand, Upanand, Krutak, Shur etc.; Madira-Aatmajah - sons of Madira; Kaushalya - Kaushalya;
Keshinam - to the son named Kesi; Tu Ekam - only one; Asut - gave birth; Kul-Nandanam - son of the family;.

From the womb of Pauravi, twelve sons were born, among whom are the names Bhut, Subhadra, Bhadrabahu, Durmad and Bhadra. From the womb of Madira, Nand, Upanand, Kritak, Shur, etc., sons were born. Kaushalya (Bhadra) had only one son who was named Keshi. Rochnayatotto jata hasta hemangadaadayah.
Ilaiyamuruvalkadinyadumukhyanajanathu. 49. Meaning of the word

Rochnayam—From Rochna, the name of the second wife; Atha—Thereafter; Jatah—Born; Hasta—Hand; Hemangad—Hemangad; Aadya—
etc.; Ilayam—From Ila, the name of the second wife; Uruvakla-Adin—Urvakla etc.; Yadu-Mukhyan—To the main men of the Yadu dynasty;
Ajijanat—Given birth.
